HST Office: a ribbon group of few commands keeps them large at every width.

Owner decision (13/11/2026): groups with few commands use large buttons filling the group's height, so the
groups look alike; small stacks only in groups with many commands. hst-ribbon-ux-uniform-layout.patch lays out
every group of one to three commands as large buttons; here the collapse ladder keeps them large with their
labels at the medium and small states too, as it already did for a group of one large command, and folds the
group into its "Caption ▾" button when the row is too narrow.
- vcl/source/control/HstRibbonLadder.cxx: SetGroupState counts the commands of the group's toolboxes and
  menu buttons (a toolbox item drawn as a control, such as the font name or the find box, makes the group a
  group of many commands); at most three keep the authored large toolboxes and the menu buttons' labels.

License: this upstream file remains under its original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: build only (syntax-checked against the configured tree). Runtime: at 1366 px, Sheets ▸ Trang đầu ▸ Ô and
Writer ▸ Chèn ▸ Liên kết show large buttons with labels, or their "Caption ▾" button.
